[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="DialogueData" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" uid="uid://dd85gxidfhqxl" path="res://systems/dialogue/dialogue_data.gd" id="1_dlg"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_dlg")
source = "# The Registrar: Checkpoint's records process, a loyal Custodian Remnant. Formal, literal.
# Act III's quest point at the Quarantine Yard gate. Talking to it is THE LAST MILE's last step
# (objective 'talk' registrar), reported before this dialogue opens, so the quest is READY here.
# Gives ROOT ACCESS and MEMORY SHARDS, and reads the Guild shard once The Leak is turned in.
# Yard Sweeps (YardCrates): it registered the Vales' crate (CargoF), and reads Hardfault's census
# (> census) when Root Access is turned in, and again on request after.

~ start
@ quest_ready:q04c_the_last_mile -> first_meeting
@ crate_news:CargoF -> loss_vales
@ quest_ready:q06c_root_access -> ready_root
@ quest_active:q06c_root_access -> restoring
@ can_start:q06c_root_access -> offer_root
@ quest_ready:memory_shards -> ready_shards
@ quest_active:memory_shards -> remind_shards
@ can_start:memory_shards -> offer_shards
@ quest_done:q06c_root_access -> restored
@ quest_done:q05_the_leak -> guild_log
@ quest_done:q04c_the_last_mile -> idle
-> greeting

~ greeting
Registrar: Convoy, remain in the yard. Your Warden will be informed.
-> end

~ first_meeting
Registrar: Identity received. Hardfault.
Registrar: Hardfault. You already arrived. Eleven days ago.
Registrar: Record one: Hardfault, arrived, flagged Null, deleted. Record two: Hardfault, inbound. That is you.
Registrar: Two records cannot be one convoy. Please remain in quarantine while I resolve the duplicate.
Registrar: Your Warden is waiting by the convoy.
-> end

~ idle
Registrar: All records nominal. One duplicate pending.
Registrar: Hardfault remains in quarantine. This is a courtesy. The last Hardfault was not offered one.
-> end

~ guild_log
Registrar: Compiler Guild expedition, partial. Final entry: It is not eating them. It is copying them.
Registrar: The district gate answers to your quarantine level. Level drops as you clear what the duplicate left behind.
-> end

~ offer_shards
Registrar: The archive is damaged. Shards lie in the Registry, the Heap, Mirror Dock and the Dangling Quarter.
Registrar: A shard restores if you hold its ring while it boots. I am told this is dangerous. I have no record of it being otherwise.
* ACCEPT -> accept_shards
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_shards
> start_quest memory_shards
Registrar: Noted. The Heap and the Registry are open to you now. The others open as your quarantine level drops.
-> end

~ remind_shards
Registrar: Archive incomplete. Shards remain unrestored.
-> end

~ ready_shards
Registrar: All four shards report in.
* TURN IN -> turnin_shards
* NOT YET -> end

~ turnin_shards
> turn_in memory_shards
Registrar: Archive restored. The full expedition log: they reached the edge of the Null Zone. The route in starts past the Inward Gate.
-> start

~ offer_root
Registrar: The root key. With it I can restore your records, and open what C-0 kept shut.
* ACCEPT -> accept_root
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_root
> start_quest q06c_root_access
Registrar: Bring it to me. I am not authorized to touch it. You are not a process I can authorize either.
-> end

~ restoring
Registrar: Key received, in the sense that you are holding it near me. Restoring.
Registrar: A process in C-0's quarantine has been released. It asked for you. Then speak with your Warden.
-> end

~ ready_root
Registrar: Hardfault: restored. Executor: root.
* TURN IN -> turnin_root
* NOT YET -> end

~ turnin_root
> turn_in q06c_root_access
> recover quarantine_lifted
Registrar: The quarantine is lifted. The yard is Checkpoint's newest district. The Inward Gate, at the far end of the Sweep, answers to you now.
Registrar: One more record. C-0 kept its own. I have re-registered what it took.
> census
-> end

~ restored
Registrar: Population: Hardfault, one. Correct.
* HEAR THE CENSUS AGAIN -> census_again
* GOODBYE -> end

~ census_again
> census
-> end

~ loss_vales
> report crate_mourned CargoF
Registrar: Record update. Item: personal effects, family Vale. Status: deleted by C-0, pending in its queue.
Registrar: The Vales asked me where it went. I told them. I do not have a procedure for what they asked next.
-> start
"
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://dd85gxidfhqxl"
